          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "HeaderToValue"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " SMT extracts specified header fields from event records, and then copies or moves the header fields to values in the event record. The "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "move"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " options removes the fields from the header entirely before adding them as values in the payload. You can configure the SMT to manipulate multiple headers in the original message. You can use dot notation to specify a node within the payload in which you want to nest the header field. For more information about configuring the SMT, see the following "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "example"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "xref",
                "target": "#example-header-to-value"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "preamble",
        "id": null,
        "outline": null,
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "To extract message headers in an event record into the record value, configure the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "HeaderToValue"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " SMT in the Kafka Connect configuration for a connector. You can configure the transformation to either remove the original headers or to copy them. To remove header fields from the record, configure the SMT to use the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "move"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " operations. To retain the header fields in the original record, configure the SMT to use the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "copy"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " operation. For example, to remove the headers "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "event_timestamp"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " and "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "key"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " from an event message, add the following lines to your connector configuration:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "transforms=moveHeadersToValue\ntransforms.moveHeadersToValue.type=io.debezium.transforms.HeaderToValue\ntransforms.moveHeadersToValue.headers=event_timestamp,key\ntransforms.moveHeadersToValue.fields=timestamp,source.id\ntransforms.moveHeadersToValue.operation=move"
              }
            ],
            "language": null,
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The following example shows the headers and values of an event record before and after the transformation is applied."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "context": "dlist",
